(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[16 1 "// Finalization (PYS9 (a); doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 218\"): pyi has no reference counts, so an object's"] [17 1 "// death is Go's collector's finding. A tracked object (one with weak references, or with a finalizer's work due: a"] [18 1 "// class's __del__, a generator's close, a socket's warning) has a Go finalizer and a record in tracked, keyed by its"] [19 1 "// address and never holding it. Go's finalizer goroutine only moves the dead object into finQueue and sets the eval"] [20 1 "// breaker's bit; the thread holding the GIL drains the queue (handleEvalBreaker, gc.collect). The order is reference"] [21 1 "// counting's (subtype_dealloc): the work first, the Go finalizer set again without it (PEP 442: once only); found"] [22 1 "// unreachable again, the weak references are cleared (in the Go finalizer, under finMu, so no weak reference yields"] [23 1 "// the object after it) and their callbacks called in CPython's list order. Go's heap does not move and an object with"] [24 1 "// a finalizer is kept until the finalizer ran, so a weak reference's hidden address is valid while it is not cleared."] [26 1 "// the work a tracked object's death runs"] [28 23 "// its class's __del__ (slot_tp_finalize)"] [29 23 "// a generator's, coroutine's or async generator's finalization (_PyGen_Finalize)"] [30 23 "// an open socket's ResourceWarning and close (sock_finalize)"] [31 23 "// an async generator's awaitable never awaited (async_gen_asend_finalize)"] [32 23 "// a built-in type's tp_finalize, the record's fin (TrackFinalizer, queue 241)"] [35 1 "// finTrack is a tracked object's record."] [37 21 "// the object's pointer's element type, to rebuild it from its address"] [38 21 "// its weak references in CPython's order: the basic ref, the basic proxy, then the newest first"] [39 21 "// the work due at its death"] [40 21 "// its identity once hashed (identityHash; an instance keeps it in its own field)"] [41 2 "// aioTask: a registered asyncio task past the strong list (builtins_asyncio.go's registry, queue 224)"] [43 2 "// owner is the interpreter that tracked it (queue 230): its work runs there, nil for the main one before any thread"] [45 2 "// fin is a built-in type's tp_finalize (workFin; queue 241), given the object: it must hold no reference to it"] [47 2 "// seq is the record's order of making (queue 253): a collection's trash is finalized in it, as CPython's lists"] [48 2 "// keep their objects in the order they were tracked"] [52 1 "// finSeq numbers the records (finMu)."] [55 1 "// finItem is a dead object's turn in the queue: obj and its work, or (obj nil) its weak references' callbacks."] [62 24 "// tracked, finQueue, the weak references' addresses (Go's finalizer goroutine takes it too)"] [65 26 "// the Go finalizers run so far (gc.collect waits until it stays still)"] [66 26 "// a drain is running (under the GIL): a nested one leaves the queue to it"] [68 18 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: nothing tracked (the weak references hold their referents, as before 218)"] [73 1 "// The moment at del (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): DELETE_FAST of a tracked object with work"] [74 1 "// or weak references due asks Go's collector at once whether that was the last reference, and drains the queue before"] [75 1 "// the next instruction: reference counting's moment when it was, a wasted collection when it was not. The collections'"] [76 1 "// time is held to a tenth of the elapsed wall time (and 50 ms); past it the death waits for the next collection."] [82 1 "// finDeletedAt is DELETE_FAST of f's fast local i (not unbound) with the check of the value it deletes. The value is"] [83 1 "// read and cleared here and dropped before anything else runs: no other variable, and no frame of a call goi"] [84 1 "// interprets, keeps it (goi's registers keep a returned call's values: queue 218's REQUEST), so that the collection"] [85 1 "// can find it dead."] [103 1 "// finPeek is the address of the value of name in d, before DELETE_NAME or DELETE_GLOBAL deletes it (0: nothing to"] [104 1 "// check); the deletion's moment is then finDeleted's, as DELETE_FAST's (queue 224: `del g` at a module's level)."] [120 1 "// finAddr is o's address for finDeleted when its holder lets it go (0: nothing to check); queue 293: sys.settrace's and"] [121 1 "// sys.setprofile's previous function, the thread's only reference to it, whose __del__ CPython runs as the call"] [122 1 "// drops it (test_sys_settrace's test_reentrancy: a __del__ that sets the trace function)."] [134 1 "// finDeleted is the check of a deleted object at address a."] [149 1 "// finVerify is the collection at a deletion: rounds while the object's record moves (its work run, then its weak"] [150 1 "// references cleared: subtype_dealloc's two steps), each a Go collection and a wait until the record moved or Go's"] [151 1 "// finalizers are still, then the drain."] [159 1 "// finVerifyRounds are finVerify's rounds; only: the drains run tr's items alone (drainOnly), the others left queued."] [195 1 "// drainOnly runs the queue's items of tr alone (queue 297: a dropped generator's close at its call's return), the"] [196 1 "// others left for the next drain, as a collection of their own would have found them: the objects the check's"] [197 1 "// collection finds dead besides (an import's module locks, say) are not run inside the caller's traced code."] [226 1 "// finQueued is whether tr's object is in the queue (finMu held)."] [236 1 "// addrOf is o's address (o a pointer: finTrackable)."] [239 1 "// hiddenPtr reads the address *u as a pointer (a weak reference's referent, alive while not cleared)."] [242 1 "// toObject is the object of type *elem at the address *u (a weak reference's referent; finMu held, *u not 0)."] [247 1 "// finTrackable is o's possible tracking: a pointer to a non-empty type of this package (another package's objects"] [248 1 "// may have their own Go finalizer, which a second SetFinalizer would abort on: _bz2's, _sqlite3's, _zstd's)."] [257 1 "// trackLocked is o's record, made (with its Go finalizer) when o has none; finMu held."] [276 1 "// trackWork tracks o (finTrackable) with the work w due at its death."] [287 1 "// TrackFinalizer is a built-in type's tp_finalize (queue 241): fin(o) runs under the GIL at o's death, once, in"] [288 1 "// __del__'s place in the order (a cycle's too). o is a pointer to a non-empty type with no Go finalizer of its own (a"] [289 1 "// type of another package may be given: pysqlite3's cursor); fin takes o as its argument and must hold no reference"] [290 1 "// to it (the record would keep it alive)."] [307 1 "// goFinalized is the Go finalizer of every tracked object, run on Go's finalizer goroutine: o into the queue."] [333 1 "// drainFinalizers runs the queue under the GIL until it is empty: the number of dead objects handled."] [360 4 "// its interpreter ended: no one to run the work in (queue 230)"] [385 2 "// the record stays (its Go finalizer set again) while weak references, new work or an identity need it"] [398 1 "// runWork runs the work w due at o's death (its record's work already cleared: PEP 442's once)."] [419 1 "// weakCallbacks calls the callbacks of a dead object's weak references, in its list's order (PyObject_ClearWeakRefs)."] [433 1 "// runDel is slot_tp_finalize: the class's __del__ called, its exception to sys.unraisablehook."] [444 1 "// finalizeGen is _PyGen_Finalize: an async generator with sys's finalizer hook handed to it; a coroutine never"] [445 1 "// started warns; a suspended generator or coroutine closed."] [465 1 "// warnUnawaitedCoroutine is _PyErr_WarnUnawaitedCoroutine: warnings._warn_unawaited_coroutine(coro), or a plain"] [466 1 "// RuntimeWarning when that failed other than by the warning itself."] [471 33 "// get_warnings_attr imports nothing at shutdown (queue 253)"] [498 1 "// finUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable from a finalizer (the object None)."] [505 1 "// finRound is one round of gc.collect: Go's collection, a wait until Go's finalizer goroutine has been still for a"] [506 1 "// moment (there is no public barrier), then the drain; the number of dead objects handled."] [523 1 "// finCollect is gc.collect's finalization: rounds until one handles nothing (at most 8), none when nothing is"] [524 1 "// tracked or queued; then the cycles through finalizers (cyCollect, queue 222) and the rounds again for what their"] [525 1 "// trash held; the number of cyclic trash nodes (CPython's count: acyclic garbage is reference counting's)."] [537 1 "// finRounds is 218's rounds: the dead objects handled."] [540 2 "// the classes' attribute caches out of date are dropped now, not at their next lookup: a stale answer (a method"] [541 2 "// deleted from its class) would keep its value alive"] [565 1 "// finalizeSocket is sock_finalize: an open socket warns ResourceWarning \"unclosed %R\" (its source the socket), then"] [566 1 "// its descriptor is closed."] [583 1 "// resourceWarn is PyErr_ResourceWarning(source, 1, msg): warnings.warn(msg, ResourceWarning, 1, source=source)."] [586 59 "// _warnings' own path at shutdown (queue 253)"] [600 1 "// growStack gives f's value stack room for n more values in a new array, the old one's values cleared: newFrame's one"] [601 1 "// allocation holds the fast locals and the stack's first array together, so the stack's stale values there would keep"] [602 1 "// their objects reachable through the fast locals for the frame's life (queue 218: found by a weak reference that a"] [603 1 "// function's first call did not clear)."] [612 1 "// pendingGens are the coroutines made, and the generators suspended in a try region, since the last flush (under the"] [613 1 "// GIL): one still not finished when the list is flushed (every 256, and in gc.collect) is tracked for its finalization,"] [614 1 "// so the common cases, a coroutine awaited at once and a generator run to its end, pay no Go finalizer (queue 218:"] [615 1 "// measured with bin/pyi aot, a coroutine 0.13 us untracked against 0.6 us tracked at creation; a generator with a"] [616 1 "// try 0.66 us against 1.0-1.2 us tracked at its first suspension)."] [619 1 "// pendCount counts the pendGen calls (queue 297): a C callable's call compares it before and after (genDropped)."] [622 1 "// callSeq counts the calls (callStack's, AotCallV's, AotCallMethodV's; queue 297): a generator made by the call just"] [623 1 "// before the one it is an argument of (madeAt) was on the value stack alone in between, never handed to another call."] [626 1 "// genSpent is genDrop.close's collections' time, held to its own tenth of the wall time (222's budget left to del)."] [638 1 "// track tracks a generator not finished for its finalization. Its frame's pointer back at it becomes an address: Go"] [639 1 "// never finalizes an object that reaches itself (queue 224: no suspended generator's frame let its generator die, so"] [640 1 "// neither close nor \"never awaited\" ran)."] [650 1 "// The moment at a call's return (queue 297; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 297\"): a generator or coroutine"] [651 1 "// suspended for the first time inside a C callable's call (any(gen()), next(f())), passed to it as an argument and held"] [652 1 "// by nothing of the calling frame, may die as the call drops its arguments, where CPython's reference counting closes it"] [653 1 "// (GeneratorExit thrown in, its finally blocks and a monitor's events run). Every call counts itself in callSeq, and a"] [654 1 "// C callable's call site compares pendCount before and after it (a load and a compare); when it moved (a generator"] [655 1 "// with a handler suspended for the first time) or while a monitor is set, genDropped takes such arguments' addresses,"] [656 1 "// the site drops its own references (callStack's frame returns first, t.drop read by its caller; a compiled call clears"] [657 1 "// its variadic array), and genDrop.close asks Go's collector at once, 222's finDeleted, its time held to the same tenth of the wall time. A"] [658 1 "// generator the frame still holds (next(g) of a local g) costs no collection: it is closed at its death as before."] [664 1 "// genDropped is the generators of args made by the call just before this one (callSeq n0), so first run by it, left"] [665 1 "// suspended where its close can be seen (a handler in its code, or a monitor set), not r (the call's value) and held"] [666 1 "// by nothing of f (frameHolds): the escape analysis that leaves the collection to the generators the frame only passed"] [667 1 "// on (any(gen()), next(f())). Each is tracked for its finalization here (one a monitor sees, without a handler, is"] [668 1 "// tracked by nothing else: its death elsewhere stays silent, as before)."] [683 1 "// close checks each generator's death at once (its finalization run when it died)."] [702 1 "// callDropped closes t.drop's generators that died (callStack's frame gone). Under goi the returned calls' slots above"] [703 1 "// its stack's top keep their values until a call takes them again (stage 0's goi; the checkout's clears them at a call's"] [704 1 "// return since c9047d52): scrubSlots takes and so clears them first."] [712 1 "// scrubSlots is n nested calls, each a window of 16 interface slots that goi clears at the call's entry (takeR); compiled,"] [713 1 "// a few nanoseconds a level."] [723 1 "// genDroppedV is genDropped over a compiled call's xs (the callable, then its arguments), the variadic array cleared"] [724 1 "// (never kept by a callee: AotCallV's rule), into t.drop: the compiled caller may still hold the arguments in its own"] [725 1 "// variables live across the call (its AotStackCall branch spills them), so the check waits for the compiled code's"] [726 1 "// next call (AotCallV's and AotCallMethodV's entry) or its return (after Native, before the frame's return events),"] [727 1 "// where they are dead."] [736 1 "// frameHolds is whether f holds o in a fast local, a cell, its stack or its namespace."] [748 79 "// self.gen"] [765 1 "// dictHolds is whether a value of d is o."] [775 1 "// generator is f's generator (f.f_generator), nil when none, or when it died first."] [802 1 "// Cycles through finalizers (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): Go never frees a cycle that"] [803 1 "// reaches a finalized object from itself, so gc.collect() finds them as CPython's gc_collect_main does, with Go's"] [804 1 "// collector answering what deduce_unreachable's counts answer: which objects are held from outside. The graph's nodes"] [805 1 "// are instances (their dictionary, while not handed out as an object, and __slots__ folded in), lists, tuples and"] [806 1 "// dictionaries; its edges their slots of interface type that hold a node. Every edge between two probed nodes is"] [807 1 "// hidden (the slot set to nil, its target kept by address), each probed node given a probe's Go finalizer, and Go"] [808 1 "// collects with the GIL held: a node whose probe does not run is held from outside, and so is what it reaches."] [811 22 "// gc.DEBUG_SAVEALL"] [812 2 "// gcDebugUncollectable is gc.DEBUG_UNCOLLECTABLE (the shutdown's garbage list printed, queue 253)"] [814 33 "// a larger graph is left alone (Go's collection, 218's moment)"] [818 35 "// a probe's answer is being read (finMu): a probe that runs later only holds"] [819 35 "// the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu), held until the collection ends"] [820 35 "// those that ran after the answer was read"] [821 35 "// tracemalloc traced once: a list, a dict or a cell may carry its Go finalizer"] [822 35 "// gc.set_debug's flags"] [823 35 "// gc.garbage"] [824 2 "// gcCollecting: a gc.collect() runs (gc.collecting: faulthandler's \"Garbage-collecting\" line, queue 241)"] [828 1 "// cyNode is a node of the graph, never holding its object (its address is hidden from the collector)."] [832 18 "// its record when tracked"] [833 18 "//