 cyVisit is cyTraverse's visitor: a slot of the node, its kind (typed: a pointer of a concrete type, else an Object)"] [939 1 "// and the node it holds."] [942 1 "// cyTraverse is tp_traverse (queue 241; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 241\"): f called with each slot of o (a"] [943 1 "// node) that holds a node. Only slots o owns alone are listed: a backing array shared with another holder would hide"] [944 1 "// that holder's reference. A reference the table does not list (a map's, a closure's, a field of a struct that is no"] [945 1 "// object) stays visible to Go's collector, which only keeps more alive."] [1013 20 "// handed out as an object: a node of its own (queue 241)"] [1020 31 "// _asyncio's Future or Task: the slots of a task's cycle (queue 224)"] [1137 1 "// cyGraph is the graph from the seeds (an object a probe would find held stays out of it), nil past cyMaxNodes."] [1183 1 "// cyRelevant is the nodes a probe must see: those of a strongly connected component with a cycle and a tracked node"] [1184 1 "// (Tarjan's, iterative), and what they reach. An acyclic dead object is Go's to find."] [1277 1 "// cyProbe asks Go's collector which of the nodes in are held from outside the set: the edges between them hidden, a"] [1278 1 "// probe's finalizer on each (a tracked node's own taken off), runtime.GC() with the GIL held, a wait until every"] [1279 1 "// probe ran or Go's finalizers are still; then the slots put back and the probes taken off. The answer: the nodes"] [1280 1 "// reachable (held from outside, or reached from such a node through the edges)."] [1300 2 "// with its probe set each node outlives its last reference: what an earlier probe held is let go now"] [1397 1 "// cyHideRegistries takes the probed nodes out of the runtime's registries that hold their keys where CPython holds"] [1398 1 "// nothing (queue 241, \"Design: 241\": the weak registries): id()'s identities of untracked objects and the functions'"] [1399 1 "// annotations. The returned function puts back the reachable nodes' entries once the answer is read; the trash's go"] [1400 1 "// (a tracked node's identity into its record), so that Go can free it."] [1434 22 "// the trash's identity in its record, should a finalizer resurrect it"] [1445 1 "// cyDebug (PYI_GC_DEBUG=1): each probe prints to stderr its nodes held from outside that no other probed node holds,"] [1446 1 "// the roots of what it keeps (queue 241: what to look at when a cycle is not found)."] [1481 1 "// cySetFinalizer gives n's object the probe's Go finalizer (a tracked node's own taken off first: Go allows one)."] [1490 1 "// cyRestore gives a surviving tracked node its own Go finalizer again (its record dropped when it needs none)."] [1507 1 "// cyClearWeakRefs clears the weak references to the trash's tracked nodes (handle_weakrefs): their callbacks, in each"] [1508 1 "// list's order, returned to be called once all are cleared (a weak reference is never a node: always \"outside\")."] [1520 24 "// a weak reference in the trash itself: no callback (handle_weakrefs)"] [1532 1 "// cyCollect is gc.collect()'s cycle detection: the trash found, PEP 442's order run over it; the number of trash nodes."] [1549 2 "// the trash in CPython's lists' order (cyOrder, queue 253): the finalizers and callbacks in a fixed order"] [1595 1 "// cySeq is a node's record's order, the untracked last."] [1603 1 "// cyCount is the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu held)."] [1623 1 "// cyFind is the cyclic trash: from the tracked nodes (or, only given, from those nodes alone: the resurrection's"] [1624 1 "// check), the graph, its relevant part probed; every probed node restored but the trash's (they keep no Go finalizer)."] [1647 1 "// cyOrder is the trash in the order CPython's lists would hold it (queue 253): its collector moves what a container"] [1648 1 "// reaches behind the container, so the trash runs from what nothing else in it holds (the dead module dictionaries"] [1649 1 "// first, in 